Spec: Plugin Source Service

Purpose:
  Resolve repository inputs, plugin names, and requested versions into a stable plugin source and installation identity.

Owns:
  ./plugin-source.ts
  ./plugin-source.test.ts

References:
  /src/cli-error.sdd
  /src/constants.sdd
  /src/git-ref.sdd

Must:
  Expand the repository shorthand `\@owner/repository` to `git@github.com:owner/repository.git`, using SSH as the default transport.
  Accept SSH URLs, SCP-style SSH repository addresses, and explicitly supplied HTTPS URLs, preserving the selected transport.
  Remove trailing slashes and one terminal `.git` suffix from the repository path when deriving repository coordinates.
  Derive repository coordinates from the lowercase hostname and every namespace and repository path segment, preserving path case.
  Include a nondefault port as `host~port` in the host coordinate to distinguish repositories served on different ports.
  Exclude transport scheme and authentication information from repository coordinates so equivalent HTTPS and SSH addresses share a destination.
  Expose @PluginSourceDescriptor.isOfficialRepository when the parsed hostname is exactly `github.com` and the first validated path segment is `specdd`, comparing both case-insensitively and requiring a following repository segment, regardless of transport or explicit port.
  Decode repository path segments only in SSH and HTTPS URLs; reject percent characters in SCP-style paths.
  Reject empty repository paths, URL queries or fragments, and decoded path components containing traversal, path separators, or characters unsafe for a local directory name before URL or path normalization can hide them.
  Require the plugin name to be one nonempty directory name, excluding `.` and `..`, path separators, and characters unsafe for a local directory name.
  Resolve the repository file path exclusively to `.plugins/<pluginname>/plugin.md`.
  Resolve its optional detached signature path to `.plugins/<pluginname>/plugin.md.asc`.
  Resolve the managed relative destination to `plugins/<repocoords>/<pluginname>/plugin.md`, relative to the registry directory.
  Preserve a supplied nonempty version verbatim as both the requested Git ref and registry `version`, including a leading `v` or a commit hash.
  Validate supplied version spelling through @isValidGitRef.
  Represent an omitted version as the remote default branch selection and registry `version` equal to `latest`.
  Provide an origin repository URL preserving the supplied path spelling and terminal suffix, with no trailing slash, HTTPS user information, or SSH password; retain an SSH username when present.

Must not:
  Perform filesystem, network, or process operations.
  Interpret versions as semantic version ranges or select GitHub releases.

Exposes:
  @PluginSource
  @PluginSource.resolve

Accepts:
  repository input
  plugin name
  optional version

Returns:
  @PluginSourceDescriptor containing transport URL, origin repository URL, repository coordinates, official-source classification, repository file and detached signature paths, managed relative destination, optional Git ref, and registry version

Raises:
  @PluginSourceError extending @CliError for invalid repository, plugin name, or version input

Scenario: GitHub shorthand
  When @PluginSource.resolve receives `\@acme/specdd-plugins`, `review`, and `v1.2.0`
  Then the repository URL is `git@github.com:acme/specdd-plugins.git`
  And the repository coordinates are `github.com/acme/specdd-plugins`
  And the source file is `.plugins/review/plugin.md`
  And the managed relative destination is `plugins/github.com/acme/specdd-plugins/review/plugin.md`
  And the registry version is `v1.2.0`

Scenario: equivalent repository transports
  When `https://github.com/acme/specdd-plugins.git` and `git@github.com:acme/specdd-plugins.git` are resolved for `review`
  Then both managed destinations are `plugins/github.com/acme/specdd-plugins/review/plugin.md`

Scenario: extensionless repository origin
  When `git@host:team/plugins` is resolved for `review`
  Then its origin repository URL remains `git@host:team/plugins`

Scenario: percent escape in an SCP path
  When `git@host:team/r%65po.git` is resolved for `review`
  Then resolution fails with @PluginSourceError

Scenario: explicit latest tag
  When the supplied version is `latest`
  Then the requested Git ref is literally `latest`
  And the registry version is `latest`

Scenario: omitted version
  When no version is supplied
  Then the remote default branch is selected
  And the registry version is `latest`

Scenario: official organization across transports
  When `\@specdd/plugins`, `git@github.com:SpecDD/plugins.git`, or `https://github.com/specdd/plugins` is resolved
  Then `isOfficialRepository` is `true`
  And lookalike hostnames or organization names are not official sources
